    "endDate": "2026-08-30T16:00:00+05:30",
    "description": "<p>MANUAL 3.0</p><p><strong>What does it look like when a craft refuses to disappear?</strong></p><p>Manual is our ongoing analog culture revival at The Commons - a space to slow down, rediscover fading crafts, and put them back into people\u2019s hands.</p><p>Manual 3.0 is about <strong>enamel painting</strong>. Meet Surabhi, an artist from Kannur who has spent years hand-painting the bold, brush-lettered signage that once covered shopfronts, walls and banners - before flex boards took over. Think Nirma ads, toothpaste walls and playful beedi art. No stencils. No digital tools. Just muscle memory and a steady hand.</p><p>Come experience an enamel painting workshop and explore his living gallery at The Commons.</p><p><em>\u201cSome crafts don't need saving. They just need a room to keep living in.\u201d</em></p><p><strong>What's the lineup?</strong><br>12:00pm \u2013 Doors open with vinyl, food &amp; drinks<br>12:30pm \u2013 Meet the artist<br>1:00pm \u2013 Explore the gallery<br>1:30\u20133:30pm \u2013 Hands-on enamel painting workshop</p><p>Come with curiosity. We\u2019ll take care of the rest.</p><p><strong>Ajji House by Subko, Bangalore | August 30th | 12pm onwards</strong></p><p>Can\u2019t make the workshop? The gallery stays live until <strong>September 5th</strong>.</p>",
